    "result_text": "That's just JaCoCo coverage exclusions for generated code \u2014 not test exclusions. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded optional `email` support to owners, following the repo's existing \"one small advice per rule\" idiom to keep structural impact low.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` string property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry the field (MapStruct auto-maps it by name \u2014 no mapper change needed).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added an `email` column plus a trivial getter/setter (each CC 1).\n- **`OwnerEmailNormalizationAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained `RequestBodyAdvice` mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephoneNormalizationAdvice`: when `email` is present it lower-cases it and rejects a syntactically invalid address with 400; an absent email is left untouched and accepted. It doesn't touch the controller or any existing handler.\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `email` column to the `owners` table.\n- **Seed data** (`hsqldb`, `mysql` `data.sql`) \u2014 appended `NULL` email to the positional owner inserts (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists, so they needed no change).\n\nI kept every changed function tiny (all CC 1) and added behavior as a new cohesive unit rather than growing the controller or an existing advice.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS (covers lower-casing on read-back, 400 on invalid, and acceptance of a missing email).",
